@ref s 2(1) "collective investment scheme" (src:1979-2192)
GIVEN
    `the participants do not have day-to-day control over the management of the property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the participants lack day-to-day control over the management of the property (whether or not they have a right to be consulted or to give directions)?
    `the property is managed as a whole by or on behalf of a manager` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the property managed as a whole by or on behalf of a manager?
    `the contributions of the participants, and the profits or income out of which payments are made to them, are pooled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the participants' contributions, and the profits or income out of which they are paid, pooled?
    `the effect of the arrangement is to enable the participants to participate in or receive profits, income, or other payments or returns from the property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the effect of the arrangement to enable the participants to participate in or receive profits, income or other payments or returns arising from the acquisition, holding, management, disposal, exercise, redemption or expiry of any right, interest, title or benefit in the property?
    `the effect of the arrangement is to enable the participants to receive sums paid out of such profits, income, or other payments or returns` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the effect of the arrangement to enable the participants to receive sums paid out of such profits, income or other payments or returns?
    `the purpose, purported purpose or purported effect of the arrangement is to enable the participants to participate in or receive profits, income, or other payments or returns from the property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose, purported purpose or purported effect of the arrangement to enable the participants to participate in or receive profits, income or other payments or returns arising from the property?
    `the purpose, purported purpose or purported effect of the arrangement is to enable the participants to receive sums paid out of such profits, income, or other payments or returns` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose, purported purpose or purported effect of the arrangement to enable the participants to receive sums paid out of such profits, income or other payments or returns?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "collective investment scheme" (a) the arrangement has the characteristics in paragraph (a)` MEANS
    IF `the participants do not have day-to-day control over the management of the property` AND (`the property is managed as a whole by or on behalf of a manager` OR `the contributions of the participants, and the profits or income out of which payments are made to them, are pooled`) AND (`the effect of the arrangement is to enable the participants to participate in or receive profits, income, or other payments or returns from the property` OR `the effect of the arrangement is to enable the participants to receive sums paid out of such profits, income, or other payments or returns` OR `the purpose, purported purpose or purported effect of the arrangement is to enable the participants to participate in or receive profits, income, or other payments or returns from the property` OR `the purpose, purported purpose or purported effect of the arrangement is to enable the participants to receive sums paid out of such profits, income, or other payments or returns`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) an arrangement in respect of any property (i) under which the participants do not have day-to-day control ...; (ii) under which either or both of the following characteristics are present ...; and (iii) under which either or both of the following characteristics are present ..."

@ref s 2(1) "collective investment scheme" (src:1979-2192)
GIVEN
    `the arrangement has the characteristics in paragraph (a) of the definition of collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the arrangement have all the characteristics of paragraph (a): participants without day-to-day control, a manager or pooling, and a profit-sharing effect or purpose?
    `the Authority has specified the arrangement, or its class or description, as a collective investment scheme by notice in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority, by notice in the Gazette, specified this arrangement (or its class or description of arrangements) as a collective investment scheme?
    `the arrangement is operated by a person otherwise than by way of business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the arrangement operated by a person otherwise than by way of business?
    `each participant carries on a business other than investment business and enters into the arrangement solely incidental to that other business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does each participant carry on a business other than investment business, and enter into the arrangement solely incidental to that other business?
    `each of the participants is a related corporation of the manager` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is each of the participants a related corporation of the manager?
    `the arrangement is made by or on behalf of an entity solely for the benefit of its directors, former directors, consultants, advisers, employees or former employees, or those of a related corporation, and their spouses, widows, widowers and children below 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the arrangement made by or on behalf of one entity solely for the benefit of persons each of whom is its (or its related corporation's) bona fide director or equivalent, former director, consultant, adviser, employee or former employee, or the spouse, widow, widower or child, adopted child or stepchild below 18 of one of them?
    `the arrangement is made by or on behalf of 2 or more entities solely for the benefit of persons each of whom is a director, former director, consultant, adviser, employee or former employee of any of them, or of a related corporation, or the spouse, widow, widower or child below 18 of one of them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the arrangement made by or on behalf of two or more entities solely for the benefit of persons each of whom is a bona fide director or equivalent, former director, consultant, adviser, employee or former employee of any of those entities (or of a related corporation of one that is a corporation), or the spouse, widow, widower or child, adopted child or stepchild below 18 of one of them?
    `the arrangement is a franchise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the arrangement a franchise as section 2(1) defines "franchise"?
    `the arrangement is one under which money is received by an advocate and solicitor from a client, acting in the ordinary course of practice, or by a statutory body as a stakeholder in carrying out its statutory functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the arrangement one under which money is received by an advocate and solicitor from a client (as stakeholder or otherwise) in the ordinary course of practice, or by a statutory body as stakeholder in carrying out its statutory functions?
    `the arrangement is made by a co-operative society registered under the Co-operative Societies Act 1979 in accordance with its objects solely for the benefit of its members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the arrangement made by a co-operative society registered under the Co-operative Societies Act 1979, in accordance with its objects, solely for the benefit of its members?
    `the arrangement is made for the purposes of a chit fund permitted to operate under the Chit Funds Act 1971` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the arrangement made for the purposes of a chit fund permitted to operate under the Chit Funds Act 1971?
    `the arrangement arises out of a life policy within the meaning of the Insurance Act 1966` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the arrangement arise out of a life policy within the meaning of the Insurance Act 1966?
    `the arrangement is a closed-end fund constituted as an entity, a sub-fund or a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the arrangement a closed-end fund (as section 2(1) defines it) constituted as an entity, a sub-fund or a trust?
    `the whole amount of each participant's contribution under the arrangement is a deposit as defined in section 4B of the Banking Act 1970` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the whole of each participant's contribution a deposit as defined in section 4B of the Banking Act 1970?
    `the predominant purpose of the arrangement is to enable the participants to share in the use or enjoyment of the property or to make its use or enjoyment available gratuitously to others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the predominant purpose of the arrangement to enable the participants to share in the use or enjoyment of the property, or to make its use or enjoyment available gratuitously to others?
    `the property consists of a currency of a country or territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the property consist of the currency of any country or territory?
    `the property consists of capital markets products` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the property consist of capital markets products?
    `the property consists of a policy as defined in the First Schedule to the Insurance Act 1966` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the property consist of a policy as defined in the First Schedule to the Insurance Act 1966?
    `the property consists of a deposit as defined in section 4B of the Banking Act 1970` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the property consist of a deposit as defined in section 4B of the Banking Act 1970?
    `the property consists of credit facilities as defined in section 2(1) of the Banking Act 1970` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the property consist of credit facilities as defined in section 2(1) of the Banking Act 1970?
    `the Authority has specified the arrangement, or its class or description, as not constituting a collective investment scheme by notice in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority, by notice in the Gazette, specified this arrangement (or its class or description of arrangements) as not constituting a collective investment scheme?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "collective investment scheme" the arrangement is a collective investment scheme` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the arrangement is operated by a person otherwise than by way of business`
           OR `each participant carries on a business other than investment business and enters into the arrangement solely incidental to that other business`
           OR `each of the participants is a related corporation of the manager`
           OR `the arrangement is made by or on behalf of an entity solely for the benefit of its directors, former directors, consultants, advisers, employees or former employees, or those of a related corporation, and their spouses, widows, widowers and children below 18`
           OR `the arrangement is made by or on behalf of 2 or more entities solely for the benefit of persons each of whom is a director, former director, consultant, adviser, employee or former employee of any of them, or of a related corporation, or the spouse, widow, widower or child below 18 of one of them`
           OR `the arrangement is a franchise`
           OR `the arrangement is one under which money is received by an advocate and solicitor from a client, acting in the ordinary course of practice, or by a statutory body as a stakeholder in carrying out its statutory functions`
           OR `the arrangement is made by a co-operative society registered under the Co-operative Societies Act 1979 in accordance with its objects solely for the benefit of its members`
           OR `the arrangement is made for the purposes of a chit fund permitted to operate under the Chit Funds Act 1971`
           OR `the arrangement arises out of a life policy within the meaning of the Insurance Act 1966`
           OR `the arrangement is a closed-end fund constituted as an entity, a sub-fund or a trust`
           OR `the whole amount of each participant's contribution under the arrangement is a deposit as defined in section 4B of the Banking Act 1970`
           OR (`the predominant purpose of the arrangement is to enable the participants to share in the use or enjoyment of the property or to make its use or enjoyment available gratuitously to others` AND (NOT (`the property consists of a currency of a country or territory` OR `the property consists of capital markets products` OR `the property consists of a policy as defined in the First Schedule to the Insurance Act 1966` OR `the property consists of a deposit as defined in section 4B of the Banking Act 1970` OR `the property consists of credit facilities as defined in section 2(1) of the Banking Act 1970`)))
           OR `the Authority has specified the arrangement, or its class or description, as not constituting a collective investment scheme by notice in the Gazette`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include (c) an arrangement operated by a person otherwise than by way of business; (d) ...; (e) ...; (f) ...; (g) ...; (h) a franchise; (i) ...; (j) ...; (k) ...; (l) ...; (m) a closed-end fund ...; (n) ...; (o) ...; (p) an arrangement ... specified by the Authority as not constituting a collective investment scheme by notice in the Gazette"
        IF `the arrangement has the characteristics in paragraph (a) of the definition of collective investment scheme` OR `the Authority has specified the arrangement, or its class or description, as a collective investment scheme by notice in the Gazette`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means (a) an arrangement in respect of any property ...; or (b) an arrangement which is an arrangement, or is of a class or description of arrangements, specified by the Authority as a collective investment scheme by notice in the Gazette"

