-- s 2(1) "closed-end fund" (aa)(i)(A): "on or after 1 July 2013".
`s 2(1) "closed-end fund" the day 1 July 2013` MEANS Date 1 7 2013

GIVEN
    `the arrangement is one referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition of collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the arrangement one referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition of "collective investment scheme" (participants without day-to-day control, a manager or pooling, a profit-sharing effect or purpose)?
    `the arrangement is one referred to in paragraph (b) of the definition of collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the arrangement one the Authority has specified as a collective investment scheme by notice in the Gazette (paragraph (b) of that definition)?
    `the units issued are exclusively or primarily non-redeemable at the election of the holders of units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the units issued exclusively or primarily non-redeemable at the election of the holders of the units?
    `the arrangement is a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the arrangement a trust?
    `the arrangement invests primarily in real estate and real estate-related assets specified by the Authority in the Code on Collective Investment Schemes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the arrangement invest primarily in real estate and real estate-related assets specified by the Authority in the Code on Collective Investment Schemes?
    `all or any of the units are listed for quotation on an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all or any of the units listed for quotation on an approved exchange?
    `the arrangement is constituted in the form of an entity, a sub-fund or as a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the arrangement constituted in the form of an entity, a sub-fund or a trust?
    `the date the arrangement was constituted` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the arrangement constituted?
    `under the investment policy, investments are made for the purpose of giving participants the benefit of the results of the investments of the arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under the arrangement's investment policy, are investments made for the purpose of giving participants the benefit of the results of the investments?
    `the arrangement carries on no business other than investment business and no activity other than one solely incidental to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the arrangement carry on no business other than investment business, and no activity other than one solely incidental to it?
    `the investment policy is clearly set out in a document provided to each participant before, or at the time, the participant first invests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the investment policy clearly set out in a document provided to each participant before, or when, the participant first invests?
    `the entity, sub-fund or trust is contractually bound to every participant to comply with the investment policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entity, sub-fund or trust contractually bound to every participant to comply with the investment policy (as amended from time to time)?
    `the investment policy sets out the types of property the arrangement may invest in and the investment guidelines or restrictions that apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the investment policy set out the types of property the arrangement is authorised to invest in, and the investment guidelines or restrictions that apply?
    `the Authority has specified by notification in the Gazette that the arrangement, or its class or description, is not a closed-end fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority, by notification in the Gazette, specified this arrangement (or its class or description) to be an arrangement that is not a closed-end fund?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "closed-end fund" the arrangement is a closed-end fund` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the arrangement is one referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition of collective investment scheme` AND `the arrangement is a trust` AND `the arrangement invests primarily in real estate and real estate-related assets specified by the Authority in the Code on Collective Investment Schemes` AND `all or any of the units are listed for quotation on an approved exchange`)
           OR (`the arrangement is one referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition of collective investment scheme`
               AND `the arrangement is constituted in the form of an entity, a sub-fund or as a trust` AND (`the date the arrangement was constituted` AT LEAST `s 2(1) "closed-end fund" the day 1 July 2013`)
               AND `under the investment policy, investments are made for the purpose of giving participants the benefit of the results of the investments of the arrangement` AND `the arrangement carries on no business other than investment business and no activity other than one solely incidental to it`
               AND (`the investment policy is clearly set out in a document provided to each participant before, or at the time, the participant first invests` OR `the entity, sub-fund or trust is contractually bound to every participant to comply with the investment policy` OR `the investment policy sets out the types of property the arrangement may invest in and the investment guidelines or restrictions that apply`))
           OR (`the arrangement is one referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition of collective investment scheme` AND `the Authority has specified by notification in the Gazette that the arrangement, or its class or description, is not a closed-end fund`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include (a) an arrangement mentioned in paragraph (a) of that definition (i) which is a trust; (ii) which invests primarily in real estate ...; and (iii) all or any units of which are listed for quotation on an approved exchange; (aa) an arrangement mentioned in paragraph (a) of that definition which (i) has all of the following characteristics ...; and (ii) has at least one of the following characteristics ...; or (b) an arrangement referred to in paragraph (a) of that definition which is ... specified by the Authority, by notification in the Gazette, to be an arrangement that is not a closed-end fund"
        IF (`the arrangement is one referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition of collective investment scheme` OR `the arrangement is one referred to in paragraph (b) of the definition of collective investment scheme`) AND `the units issued are exclusively or primarily non-redeemable at the election of the holders of units`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means an arrangement referred to in paragraph (a) or (b) of the definition of collective investment scheme under which units that are issued are exclusively or primarily non-redeemable at the election of the holders of units"

-- src:1975 | “Code on Collective Investment Schemes” means the Code on
-- src:1976 | Collective Investment Schemes referred to in section 284
-- src:1977 | which is issued by the Authority under section 321(1);
@ref s 2(1) "Code on Collective Investment Schemes" (src:1975-1977)
GIVEN
    `the document is the Code on Collective Investment Schemes referred to in section 284 and issued by the Authority under section 321(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document the Code on Collective Investment Schemes referred to in section 284 and issued by the Authority under section 321(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "Code on Collective Investment Schemes" the document is the Code on Collective Investment Schemes` MEANS
    IF `the document is the Code on Collective Investment Schemes referred to in section 284 and issued by the Authority under section 321(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means the Code on Collective Investment Schemes referred to in section 284 which is issued by the Authority under section 321(1)"

-- src:2260 | “custodian”, in relation to a collective investment scheme
-- src:2261 | constituted as a VCC or sub‑fund, means an entity to which
-- src:2262 | the assets of the scheme are entrusted for safekeeping;
@ref s 2(1) "custodian" (src:2260-2262)
GIVEN
    `the collective investment scheme is constituted as a VCC or sub-fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the collective investment scheme constituted as a VCC or sub-fund?
    `the assets of the scheme are entrusted to the entity for safekeeping` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the assets of the scheme entrusted to the entity for safekeeping?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "custodian" the entity is a custodian of the scheme` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the collective investment scheme is constituted as a VCC or sub-fund`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to a collective investment scheme constituted as a VCC or sub-fund"
        IF `the assets of the scheme are entrusted to the entity for safekeeping`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means an entity to which the assets of the scheme are entrusted for safekeeping"

-- src:2690 | “manager”, in relation to a collective investment scheme, means
-- src:2691 | a person, by whatever name called, who is responsible for
-- src:2692 | managing the property of, or operating, the collective
-- src:2693 | investment scheme;
@ref s 2(1) "manager" (src:2690-2693)
GIVEN
    `the person, by whatever name called, is responsible for managing the property of, or operating, the collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person (by whatever name called) responsible for managing the property of, or operating, the collective investment scheme?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "manager" the person is the manager of the collective investment scheme` MEANS
    IF `the person, by whatever name called, is responsible for managing the property of, or operating, the collective investment scheme`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a person, by whatever name called, who is responsible for managing the property of, or operating, the collective investment scheme"

-- s 2(1) "participant": the Act gives a different meaning for Part 2, Part 2A, Part 3 and every other provision.
DECLARE `s 2(1) "participant" provision read` IS ONE OF
    `s 2(1) "participant" for Part 2`
    `s 2(1) "participant" for Part 2A`
    `s 2(1) "participant" for Part 3`
    `s 2(1) "participant" for any other provision`

-- src:2724 | “participant” means —
-- src:2726 | (a) for the purposes of Part 2, a person who may
-- src:2727 | participate in one or more of the services provided
-- src:2728 | by an approved exchange or a recognised market
-- src:2729 | operator, in its capacity as an approved exchange or a
-- src:2730 | recognised market operator, as the case may be;
-- src:2732 | (aa) for the purposes of Part 2A, a person who may
-- src:2733 | participate in one or more of the services provided by
-- src:2734 | a licensed trade repository or licensed foreign trade
-- src:2735 | repository, in its capacity as a licensed trade
-- src:2736 | repository or licensed foreign trade repository, as
-- src:2737 | the case may be;
-- src:2739 | (b) for the purposes of Part 3, a person who, under the
-- src:2740 | business rules of an approved clearing house or a
-- src:2741 | recognised clearing house, may participate in one or
-- src:2742 | more of the services provided by the approved
-- src:2743 | clearing house or recognised clearing house, in its
-- src:2744 | capacity as an approved clearing house or a
-- src:2745 | recognised clearing house, as the case may be; or
-- src:2747 | (c) for the purposes of any other provision of this Act, a
-- src:2748 | person who participates in a collective investment
-- src:2749 | scheme by way of owning one or more units in a
-- src:2750 | collective investment scheme;
@ref s 2(1) "participant" (src:2724-2750)
GIVEN
    `the provision being read` IS A `s 2(1) "participant" provision read` @desc Which provision is the word "participant" being read for: Part 2, Part 2A, Part 3, or any other provision?
    `the person may participate in one or more of the services provided by an approved exchange or recognised market operator in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May the person participate in one or more of the services an approved exchange or recognised market operator provides in that capacity?
    `the person may participate in one or more of the services provided by a licensed trade repository or licensed foreign trade repository in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May the person participate in one or more of the services a licensed trade repository or licensed foreign trade repository provides in that capacity?
    `the person may, under the business rules of an approved clearing house or recognised clearing house, participate in one or more of the services it provides in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May the person, under the business rules of an approved clearing house or recognised clearing house, participate in one or more of the services it provides in that capacity?
    `the person participates in a collective investment scheme by owning one or more units in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person participate in a collective investment scheme by owning one or more units in it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "participant" the person is a participant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision being read`
    WHEN `s 2(1) "participant" for Part 2`
        THEN IF `the person may participate in one or more of the services provided by an approved exchange or recognised market operator in that capacity`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) for the purposes of Part 2, a person who may participate in one or more of the services provided by an approved exchange or a recognised market operator"
    WHEN `s 2(1) "participant" for Part 2A`
        THEN IF `the person may participate in one or more of the services provided by a licensed trade repository or licensed foreign trade repository in that capacity`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(aa) for the purposes of Part 2A, a person who may participate in one or more of the services provided by a licensed trade repository or licensed foreign trade repository"
    WHEN `s 2(1) "participant" for Part 3`
        THEN IF `the person may, under the business rules of an approved clearing house or recognised clearing house, participate in one or more of the services it provides in that capacity`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) for the purposes of Part 3, a person who, under the business rules of an approved clearing house or a recognised clearing house, may participate in one or more of the services"
    WHEN `s 2(1) "participant" for any other provision`
        THEN IF `the person participates in a collective investment scheme by owning one or more units in it`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) for the purposes of any other provision of this Act, a person who participates in a collective investment scheme by way of owning one or more units"

-- s 2(1) "responsible person": the three ways a scheme can be constituted, and the three answers.
DECLARE `s 2(1) "responsible person" how the scheme is constituted` IS ONE OF
    `s 2(1) "responsible person" a VCC or a sub-fund`
    `s 2(1) "responsible person" a corporation other than a VCC`
    `s 2(1) "responsible person" some other way`

DECLARE `s 2(1) "responsible person" who it is` IS ONE OF
    `s 2(1) "responsible person" the VCC`
    `s 2(1) "responsible person" the corporation`
    `s 2(1) "responsible person" the manager for the scheme`

-- src:3047 | “responsible person”, in relation to a collective investment
-- src:3048 | scheme, means —
-- src:3050 | (a) in the case of a scheme that is constituted as a VCC or
-- src:3051 | a sub‑fund — the VCC;
-- src:3053 | (b) in the case of a scheme that is constituted as a
-- src:3054 | corporation other than a VCC — the corporation; or
-- src:3056 | (c) in the case of any other scheme — the manager for
-- src:3057 | the scheme;
@ref s 2(1) "responsible person" (src:3047-3057)
GIVEN
    `how the collective investment scheme is constituted` IS A `s 2(1) "responsible person" how the scheme is constituted` @desc How is the collective investment scheme constituted: as a VCC or a sub-fund, as a corporation other than a VCC, or in some other way?
GIVETH A `s 2(1) "responsible person" who it is`
`s 2(1) "responsible person" who is the responsible person of the scheme` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the collective investment scheme is constituted`
    WHEN `s 2(1) "responsible person" a VCC or a sub-fund` THEN `s 2(1) "responsible person" the VCC`
    WHEN `s 2(1) "responsible person" a corporation other than a VCC` THEN `s 2(1) "responsible person" the corporation`
    WHEN `s 2(1) "responsible person" some other way` THEN `s 2(1) "responsible person" the manager for the scheme`

-- src:2881 | “real estate investment trust”, except in Division 3 of Part 7,
-- src:2882 | means a collective investment scheme —
-- src:2884 | (a) that is authorised under section 286 or recognised
-- src:2885 | under section 287;
-- src:2887 | (b) that is a trust;
-- src:2889 | (c) that invests primarily in real estate and real
-- src:2890 | estate‑related assets specified by the Authority in
-- src:2891 | the Code on Collective Investment Schemes; and
-- src:2893 | (d) all or any units of which are listed for quotation on an
-- src:2894 | approved exchange;
@ref s 2(1) "real estate investment trust" (src:2881-2894)
GIVEN
    `the provision being read is in Division 3 of Part 7` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision you are reading in Division 3 of Part 7?
    `the scheme is a collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the scheme a collective investment scheme as section 2(1) defines it?
    `the scheme is authorised under section 286 or recognised under section 287` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the scheme authorised under section 286 or recognised under section 287?
    `the scheme is a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the scheme a trust?
    `the scheme invests primarily in real estate and real estate-related assets specified by the Authority in the Code on Collective Investment Schemes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the scheme invest primarily in real estate and real estate-related assets specified by the Authority in the Code on Collective Investment Schemes?
    `all or any of the units of the scheme are listed for quotation on an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all or any of the scheme's units listed for quotation on an approved exchange?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "real estate investment trust" the scheme is a real estate investment trust` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the provision being read is in Division 3 of Part 7`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except in Division 3 of Part 7"
        IF `the scheme is a collective investment scheme` AND `the scheme is authorised under section 286 or recognised under section 287` AND `the scheme is a trust` AND `the scheme invests primarily in real estate and real estate-related assets specified by the Authority in the Code on Collective Investment Schemes` AND `all or any of the units of the scheme are listed for quotation on an approved exchange`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a collective investment scheme (a) that is authorised under section 286 or recognised under section 287; (b) that is a trust; (c) that invests primarily in real estate and real estate-related assets ...; and (d) all or any units of which are listed for quotation on an approved exchange"

-- src:2896 | “real estate investment trust management” has the meaning
-- src:2897 | given in the Second Schedule;
@ref s 2(1) "real estate investment trust management" (src:2896-2897)
GIVEN
    `the activity meets the Second Schedule meaning of real estate investment trust management` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the activity meet the meaning of "real estate investment trust management" that the Second Schedule gives?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "real estate investment trust management" the activity is real estate investment trust management` MEANS
    IF `the activity meets the Second Schedule meaning of real estate investment trust management`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has the meaning given in the Second Schedule"

§ `s 2(1): units, unitholders, voting units and substantial unitholders`

-- src:3401 | “unit” —
-- src:3403 | (a) in relation to a collective investment scheme, means a
-- src:3404 | right or interest (however described) in a collective
-- src:3405 | investment scheme (whether or not constituted as an
-- src:3406 | entity), and includes an option to acquire any such
-- src:3407 | right or interest in the collective investment scheme;
-- src:3408 | and
-- src:3410 | (b) in relation to a business trust, has the meaning given
-- src:3411 | by section 2 of the Business Trusts Act 2004;
@ref s 2(1) "unit" (src:3401-3411)
GIVEN
    `the thing is a right or interest, however described, in a collective investment scheme, whether or not constituted as an entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a right or interest (however described) in a collective investment scheme, whether or not the scheme is constituted as an entity?
    `the thing is an option to acquire such a right or interest in the collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing an option to acquire such a right or interest in the collective investment scheme?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "unit" (a) the right or interest is a unit in a collective investment scheme` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a right or interest, however described, in a collective investment scheme, whether or not constituted as an entity` OR `the thing is an option to acquire such a right or interest in the collective investment scheme`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to a collective investment scheme, means a right or interest (however described) in a collective investment scheme (whether or not constituted as an entity), and includes an option to acquire any such right or interest"

GIVEN
    `the thing is a unit within section 2 of the Business Trusts Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a unit in a business trust as section 2 of the Business Trusts Act 2004 defines "unit"?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "unit" (b) the thing is a unit in a business trust` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a unit within section 2 of the Business Trusts Act 2004`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to a business trust, has the meaning given by section 2 of the Business Trusts Act 2004"

-- src:3413 | “unitholder” —
-- src:3415 | (a) in relation to a collective investment scheme, means a
-- src:3416 | participant of the scheme; and
-- src:3418 | (b) in relation to a business trust, means a person who
-- src:3419 | holds a unit in the business trust;
@ref s 2(1) "unitholder" (src:3413-3419)
GIVEN
    `the person is a participant of the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a participant of the scheme?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "unitholder" (a) the person is a unitholder of a collective investment scheme` MEANS
    IF `the person is a participant of the scheme`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to a collective investment scheme, means a participant of the scheme"

GIVEN
    `the person holds a unit in the business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person hold a unit in the business trust?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "unitholder" (b) the person is a unitholder of a business trust` MEANS
    IF `the person holds a unit in the business trust`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to a business trust, means a person who holds a unit in the business trust"

-- s 2(1) "voting unit": the circumstances in which a unit may carry a vote.
-- The six listed circumstances are the ones that do NOT make a unit a voting unit when they are the only ones;
-- "any other circumstance" is a vote in a circumstance the list does not name.
DECLARE `s 2(1) "voting unit" circumstance of a vote` IS ONE OF
    `s 2(1) "voting unit" a vote while a distribution is in arrears`
    `s 2(1) "voting unit" a vote on a proposal to reduce the unitholders' equity or the participants' funds`
    `s 2(1) "voting unit" a vote on a proposal that affects rights attached to the unit`
    `s 2(1) "voting unit" a vote on a proposal to wind up the business trust or the scheme`
    `s 2(1) "voting unit" a vote on a proposal to dispose of the whole of the property, business and undertakings`
    `s 2(1) "voting unit" a vote during the winding up`
    `s 2(1) "voting unit" a vote in any other circumstance`

GIVEN `the circumstances` IS A LIST OF `s 2(1) "voting unit" circumstance of a vote` @desc In which circumstances does the unit carry a right to vote? (An empty list: in none.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "voting unit" the unit carries a vote in some circumstance the definition does not list` MEANS
    any (GIVEN c YIELD c EQUALS `s 2(1) "voting unit" a vote in any other circumstance`) `the circumstances`

-- src:3463 | “voting unit” —
-- src:3465 | (a) in relation to a business trust, means an issued unit in
-- src:3466 | the business trust, other than —
-- src:3468 | (i) a unit to which in no circumstances is there
-- src:3469 | attached a right to vote; or
-- src:3471 | (ii) a unit to which there is attached a right to vote
-- src:3472 | only in one or more of the following
-- src:3473 | circumstances:
-- src:3475 | (A) during a period in which a distribution (or
-- src:3476 | part of a distribution) in respect of the
-- src:3477 | unit is in arrears;
-- src:3479 | (B) upon a proposal to reduce the
-- src:3480 | unitholders’ equity of the business trust;
-- src:3482 | (C) upon a proposal that affects rights
-- src:3483 | attached to the unit;
-- src:3485 | (D) upon a proposal to wind up the business
-- src:3486 | trust;
-- src:3491 | (E) upon a proposal for the disposal of the
-- src:3492 | whole of the property, business and
-- src:3493 | undertakings of the business trust;
-- src:3495 | (F) during the winding up of the business
-- src:3496 | trust; and
-- src:3498 | (b) in relation to a collective investment scheme, means
-- src:3499 | an issued unit in the scheme, other than —
-- src:3501 | (i) a unit to which in no circumstances is there
-- src:3502 | attached a right to vote; or
-- src:3504 | (ii) a unit to which there is attached a right to vote
-- src:3505 | only in one or more of the following
-- src:3506 | circumstances:
-- src:3508 | (A) during a period in which a distribution (or
-- src:3509 | part of a distribution) in respect of the
-- src:3510 | unit is in arrears;
-- src:3512 | (B) upon a proposal to reduce the
-- src:3513 | participants’ funds of the scheme;
-- src:3515 | (C) upon a proposal that affects rights
-- src:3516 | attached to the unit;
-- src:3518 | (D) upon a proposal to wind up the scheme;
-- src:3520 | (E) upon a proposal for the disposal of the
-- src:3521 | whole of the property, business and
-- src:3522 | undertakings of the scheme;
-- src:3524 | (F) during the winding up of the scheme.
@ref s 2(1) "voting unit" (src:3463-3524)
GIVEN
    `the unit has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the unit been issued?
    `the circumstances in which a right to vote is attached to the unit` IS A LIST OF `s 2(1) "voting unit" circumstance of a vote` @desc In which circumstances is a right to vote attached to the unit? (None, or any of: while a distribution is in arrears; on a proposal to reduce the equity or funds; on a proposal that affects rights attached to the unit; on a proposal to wind up; on a proposal to dispose of the whole of the property, business and undertakings; during the winding up; or any other circumstance.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "voting unit" (a) the unit is a voting unit in a business trust` MEANS
    IF `the unit has been issued` AND `s 2(1) "voting unit" the unit carries a vote in some circumstance the definition does not list` `the circumstances in which a right to vote is attached to the unit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means an issued unit ..., other than (i) a unit to which in no circumstances is there attached a right to vote; or (ii) a unit to which there is attached a right to vote only in one or more of the following circumstances"

GIVEN
    `the unit has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the unit been issued?
    `the circumstances in which a right to vote is attached to the unit` IS A LIST OF `s 2(1) "voting unit" circumstance of a vote` @desc In which circumstances is a right to vote attached to the unit? (None, or any of: while a distribution is in arrears; on a proposal to reduce the equity or funds; on a proposal that affects rights attached to the unit; on a proposal to wind up; on a proposal to dispose of the whole of the property, business and undertakings; during the winding up; or any other circumstance.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "voting unit" (b) the unit is a voting unit in a collective investment scheme` MEANS
    IF `the unit has been issued` AND `s 2(1) "voting unit" the unit carries a vote in some circumstance the definition does not list` `the circumstances in which a right to vote is attached to the unit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means an issued unit ..., other than (i) a unit to which in no circumstances is there attached a right to vote; or (ii) a unit to which there is attached a right to vote only in one or more of the following circumstances"

-- src:3166 | “substantial unitholder” —
-- src:3168 | (a) in relation to a collective investment scheme, means a
-- src:3169 | participant who has an interest or interests in one or
-- src:3170 | more voting units in the scheme, the total votes
-- src:3171 | attached to that unit, or those units, being not less
-- src:3172 | than 5% of the total votes attached to all the voting
-- src:3173 | units in the scheme; or
-- src:3175 | (b) in relation to a business trust, means a person who has
-- src:3176 | an interest or interests in one or more voting units in
-- src:3177 | the business trust, the total votes attached to that unit,
-- src:3178 | or those units, being not less than 5% of the total
-- src:3179 | votes attached to all the voting units in the business
-- src:3180 | trust;
@ref s 2(1) "substantial unitholder" (src:3166-3180)
GIVEN
    `the person is a participant in the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a participant in the scheme?
    `the person has an interest in one or more voting units in the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have an interest (as section 4 treats it) in one or more voting units in the scheme?
    `the total votes attached to the voting units the person has an interest in` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes in total are attached to the voting units the person has an interest in?
    `the total votes attached to all the voting units in the scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes in total are attached to all the voting units in the scheme?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "substantial unitholder" (a) the participant is a substantial unitholder of a collective investment scheme` MEANS
    IF `the person is a participant in the scheme` AND `the person has an interest in one or more voting units in the scheme` AND `the total votes attached to the voting units the person has an interest in` AT LEAST (`the total votes attached to all the voting units in the scheme` TIMES 5%)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to a collective investment scheme, means a participant who has an interest or interests in one or more voting units in the scheme, the total votes attached to that unit, or those units, being not less than 5% of the total votes attached to all the voting units in the scheme"

GIVEN
    `the person has an interest in one or more voting units in the business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have an interest (as section 4 treats it) in one or more voting units in the business trust?
    `the total votes attached to the voting units the person has an interest in` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes in total are attached to the voting units the person has an interest in?
    `the total votes attached to all the voting units in the business trust` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes in total are attached to all the voting units in the business trust?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "substantial unitholder" (b) the person is a substantial unitholder of a business trust` MEANS
    IF `the person has an interest in one or more voting units in the business trust` AND `the total votes attached to the voting units the person has an interest in` AT LEAST (`the total votes attached to all the voting units in the business trust` TIMES 5%)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to a business trust, means a person who has an interest or interests in one or more voting units in the business trust, the total votes attached to that unit, or those units, being not less than 5% of the total votes attached to all the voting units in the business trust"

§ `s 2(1): business trusts and trustee-managers`

-- src:1856 | “business trust” has the meaning given by section 2 of the
-- src:1857 | Business Trusts Act 2004;
@ref s 2(1) "business trust" (src:1856-1857)
GIVEN
    `the trust is a business trust within section 2 of the Business Trusts Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust a business trust as section 2 of the Business Trusts Act 2004 defines the term?
