`s 2(1) "trustee-manager" the person is the trustee-manager of the business trust` MEANS
    IF `the person is the trustee-manager of a registered business trust within section 2 of the Business Trusts Act 2004` OR `the company is the one proposed to be named as the trustee-manager in an application for registration under section 4(1) of the Business Trusts Act 2004` OR `the entity manages and operates the recognised business trust, by whatever name called and whether incorporated or not` OR `the entity is proposed to be managing and operating the business trust in an application for recognition under section 239D(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) in relation to a registered business trust, has the meaning given by section 2 of the Business Trusts Act 2004; (b) ... means the company proposed to be named as the trustee-manager in the application ...; (c) ... means the entity which manages and operates the recognised business trust ...; and (d) ... means the entity proposed to be managing and operating the trust"

